{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "All implementation will target Java 17+ and Spring Framework 6.0+ as per the framework's current requirements.",
    "For reliable HDFS writes (U2), the HDFS sync() API will be used to confirm data is persisted to disk before sending an acknowledgement to the message bus, with retry logic for failed commits.",
    "For partition function override (U3), a strategy pattern will be used, with a new PartitionStrategy interface that users can implement and configure via module properties to override the default partitioner.",
    "For multi topic-partition consumption (U4), the existing Kafka consumer will be extended to support multiple topic-partition assignments per instance, with a thread-safe blocking queue used to aggregate messages from all assigned partitions into a single consumer queue.",
    "For the Flo DSL parser (U5), a context registry will be added to the parser to store previously parsed stream definitions, enabling validation of cross-stream references and module/option values against existing stream context.",
    "For single container stream deployment (U6), Docker will be used for containerization, with a shared Docker network and shared volumes for inter-module communication and data persistence, respectively.",
    "For non-default ConfigurableConversionService tuples (U7), custom Jackson deserialization logic will be added for ConfigurableConversionService beans to preserve non-default converter configurations during deserialization.",
    "For JMX benchmarking (U8), JMH (Java Microbenchmark Harness) will be used for isolated performance testing, with test scenarios covering both JMX enabled and disabled states, measuring throughput and end-to-end latency."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "All required third-party dependencies (HDFS client, Kafka client, JMH, Flo UI integration libraries) are already managed in the project's dependency management system and do not require additional version negotiation.",
    "Existing project test infrastructure (unit test frameworks, integration test environments, CI/CD pipelines) is fully functional and does not require modifications to support the new functionality.",
    "The BaseDefinition class referenced in U1 is part of the current active codebase and can be modified without impacting unrelated modules outside the scope of this increment.",
    "A test HDFS cluster and test Kafka cluster are available in the development environment for integration testing of U2 and U4, respectively.",
    "The Flo UI development team will provide required integration points and sample UI payloads for the new DSL parser (U5) within the development timeline.",
    "A dedicated test environment with JMX monitoring tools is available for running the JMX benchmarks required for U8.",
    "All changes implemented for this increment will maintain backward compatibility with existing public APIs, so no additional migration guides or deprecation work is required.",
    "The project's existing code review and merge process will be handled by other team members, so no effort is allocated for those activities."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "U1: Analyze BaseDefinition module list usage",
      "activity_description": "Review current BaseDefinition implementation, identify all references to the module list field, assess impact of removing the field and implementing on-demand reparse logic.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1: Implement BaseDefinition reparse logic",
      "activity_description": "Remove the module list field from BaseDefinition, implement on-demand reparse of module definitions when required, update all dependent classes to use the new reparse mechanism.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U1: Test BaseDefinition changes",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests for the reparse logic, run full integration test suite to verify no regressions in existing module loading and stream deployment functionality.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U2: Design HDFS commit acknowledgement flow",
      "activity_description": "Design integration between HDFS sync commit API and existing message bus acknowledgement mechanism, define ack message format and retry logic for failed HDFS commits.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U2: Implement HDFS reliable write logic",
      "activity_description": "Implement HDFS write logic with sync commit, add acknowledgement emission to the message bus upon successful HDFS commit, implement retry and error handling for failed commits.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U2: Test HDFS reliable write functionality",
      "activity_description": "Write integration tests using a test HDFS cluster, verify acknowledgements are only sent after successful HDFS commit, test failure, retry, and edge case scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U3: Design partition function override mechanism",
      "activity_description": "Design the configurable partition strategy interface, define how users can specify custom partition functions via module configuration, align with existing module property handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U3: Implement partition function override",
      "activity_description": "Add configurable partition strategy field to source and processor module base classes, implement logic to use custom partition function if provided, fall back to default partitioner if not configured.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U3: Test partition function override",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests for custom partition function usage, test fallback to default partitioner, verify data is correctly routed to the specified partitions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U4: Design multi topic-partition consumption flow",
      "activity_description": "Design consumer configuration to support multiple topic-partition assignments per instance, design thread-safe message aggregation logic to combine messages from all partitions into a single internal queue.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U4: Implement multi topic-partition consumer",
      "activity_description": "Extend existing Kafka consumer to support multiple topic-partition subscriptions, implement message aggregation into a single thread-safe queue, handle offset management for multiple assigned partitions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "U4: Test multi topic-partition consumption",
      "activity_description": "Write integration tests using a test Kafka cluster, verify messages from multiple topic-partitions are correctly aggregated into a single queue, test offset commit and failure scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "U5: Design extended DSL parser with context registry",
      "activity_description": "Design context registry to store parsed stream definitions, design validation logic to check module/option values against existing stream context to detect cross-stream reference errors.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "U5: Implement extended DSL parser and validation",
      "activity_description": "Extend existing DSL parser to populate the context registry during parsing, add validation steps for module/option values against registered context, implement error handling for invalid cross-stream references.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "U5: Integrate and test DSL parser with Flo UI",
      "activity_description": "Integrate the new parser with Flo UI's existing parsing flow, write unit and integration tests for the provided example use case, verify incorrect module/option values are detected correctly.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "U6: Research single container deployment options",
      "activity_description": "Research container orchestration options for colocating stream modules, evaluate network and volume configuration requirements for inter-module communication and data sharing.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "U6: Design single container deployment architecture",
      "activity_description": "Design container layout for colocated stream modules, define shared resource configuration, document deployment steps, constraints, and known limitations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A18",
      "activity_name": "U6: Document and review deployment approach",
      "activity_description": "Create formal documentation for the single container deployment approach, include architecture diagrams, configuration examples, and operational guidance, incorporate stakeholder feedback.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A19",
      "activity_name": "U7: Analyze conversion service deserialization issue",
      "activity_description": "Review current deserialization logic for ConfigurableConversionService beans, identify root cause of non-default tuples being reset after deserialization, assess impact on existing functionality.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A20",
      "activity_name": "U7: Implement conversion service tuple preservation",
      "activity_description": "Implement custom Jackson deserialization logic for ConfigurableConversionService to preserve non-default converter configurations, update all relevant deserialization paths to use the new logic.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A21",
      "activity_name": "U7: Test conversion service tuple preservation",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests to verify non-default conversion service configurations are preserved after deserialization, test edge cases with custom converters and complex tuple configurations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A22",
      "activity_name": "U8: Design JMX benchmark test scenarios",
      "activity_description": "Define benchmark test cases for stream processing with JMX enabled and disabled, identify key performance metrics (throughput, latency) to measure, define test data and load parameters.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A23",
      "activity_name": "U8: Implement and run JMX benchmarks",
      "activity_description": "Set up JMH benchmark tests for the defined scenarios, run benchmarks in a controlled test environment, collect and raw performance data for both JMX states.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A24",
      "activity_name": "U8: Document benchmark results",
      "activity_description": "Analyze collected benchmark data, document performance differences between JMX enabled and disabled states, include recommendations for JMX usage in production environments.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 61
  }
}

